---
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import { PromptBlock } from "../components/PromptBlock";
import { StepNav } from "../components/StepNav";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { LEADER_NOTES, PROMPTS, REPO_URL, SITE, STEPS } from "../lib/site";

const stepByIndex = (i: number) => STEPS[i];
---

<BaseLayout>
	<Hero slot="hero" />
	<StepNav slot="nav" client:load />

	<div class="leader-toolbar">
		<button type="button" id="leader-toggle" class="leader-toggle-btn">
			🎤 Hide leader notes
		</button>
	</div>

	<section class="intro-card">
		<h2 class="intro-title">What you'll learn</h2>
		<p class="intro-body">{SITE.description}</p>
		<div class="intro-legend">
			<div class="legend-item">
				<span class="legend-badge legend-badge--why">Why</span>
				<span>The concept behind the step</span>
			</div>
			<div class="legend-item">
				<span class="legend-badge legend-badge--do">Do</span>
				<span>The action you (or your agent) takes</span>
			</div>
			<div class="legend-item">
				<span class="legend-badge legend-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<span>What success looks like</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{/* ─── Step 0: Prereqs ─── */}
	<article id="prereqs" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(0).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(0).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(0).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Gather these four things before you start. Nothing scary — most you probably already have.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="checklist">
				<div class="checklist-item">
					<span class="checklist-icon" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
					<div>
						<p class="checklist-title">Node.js, git, and a terminal</p>
						<p class="checklist-note">Standard developer setup.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="checklist-item">
					<span class="checklist-icon" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
					<div>
						<p class="checklist-title">A coding agent</p>
						<p class="checklist-note">Whatever you already use. <a href="https://opencode.ai">OpenCode</a> works if you don't have one.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="checklist-item">
					<span class="checklist-icon" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
					<div>
						<p class="checklist-title">A GitHub account</p>
						<p class="checklist-note">The deploy button creates a repo in it.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="checklist-item">
					<span class="checklist-icon" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
					<div>
						<p class="checklist-title">A free Cloudflare account</p>
						<p class="checklist-note">No credit card required. <a href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up">Sign up</a> now — one less thing to do mid-step.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="tip">
				<span class="tip-label">Recommended</span>
				<p><a href="https://cli.github.com/">GitHub CLI</a> (<code>gh</code>), authenticated — your agent opens the pull request for you in Step 3. Without it, your agent will hand you a link to open the PR yourself. Install with <code>brew install gh</code>, then run <code>gh auth login</code>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.prereqs?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 1: Deploy ─── */}
	<article id="deploy" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(1).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(1).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(1).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">One click. A repo in your account, a database, and a production Worker — wired up for you.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--why">Why</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>You need a real, deployed app before you can create a Preview of it. The deploy button skips the manual setup.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Clicking the button below will:</p>
					<ul class="tight-list">
						<li>Fork the app repo into your GitHub account</li>
						<li>Provision a production D1 database</li>
						<li>Connect <strong>Workers Builds</strong> (Cloudflare's CI/CD) to that repo</li>
						<li>Deploy the Worker</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="phase-note">No custom GitHub Actions to set up, no secrets to paste — automatic.</p>

					<div class="deploy-cta-wrap">
						<a
							href={`https://deploy.workers.cloudflare.com/?url=${REPO_URL}`}
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							class="deploy-cta-link"
						>
							<img src="https://deploy.workers.cloudflare.com/button" alt="Deploy to Cloudflare" />
						</a>
					</div>
					<p class="phase-note">If signing in drops you on the template picker, choose <strong>Clone a public repository via Git URL</strong> and enter <code>{REPO_URL}</code>.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Open the production URL Cloudflare gives you. You should see an <strong>Activity Log</strong> with three seeded entries. Remember what's in there — you'll compare it against your Preview shortly.</p>
					<Figure
						src="/screenshots/app-production-seeded.png"
						alt="The production Activity Log showing three seeded entries: Wired up Workers Builds, Provisioned the D1 database, and Deployed the production Worker."
						caption="Your production app — three seeded rows. This is the data your Preview will not have."
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="step-next">
				<a href="#isolate" class="step-next-link">
					<span class="step-next-hint">Next</span>
					Isolate a resource
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.deploy?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 2: Isolate ─── */}
	<article id="isolate" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(2).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(2).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(2).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Give every Preview a production-safe D1 binding and its own observability settings.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Setup</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>First, get the repo onto your machine and make a branch:</p>
					<div class="cmd">
						<div class="cmd-bar"><span class="cmd-label">Terminal</span></div>
						<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/&lt;you&gt;/d1-template-preview.git
cd d1-template-preview
npm install
npx wrangler login
npx wrangler whoami
git checkout -b isolate-preview-db</code></pre>
					</div>
					<p class="phase-note">Confirm <code>wrangler whoami</code> lists the Cloudflare account you used in Step 1. If it lists multiple accounts, set <code>CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID</code> to that account's ID for the rest of this terminal session.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--why">Why</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>
						Previews inherit your <strong>code</strong> automatically. Their variables, secrets, bindings, and observability come from separate Preview configuration, so production resources are never used accidentally.
					</p>

					<div class="concept-diagram">
						<div class="concept-col">
							<span class="concept-col-head concept-col-head--prod">Production</span>
							<div class="concept-cell">code</div>
							<div class="concept-cell concept-cell--bind">DB → prod-db</div>
						</div>
						<div class="concept-col">
							<span class="concept-col-head concept-col-head--preview">Preview</span>
							<div class="concept-cell concept-cell--inherit">code (inherited)</div>
							<div class="concept-cell concept-cell--empty">DB → ??? (empty!)</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<p>D1, KV, R2, and most other resources bind by ID. You will create one D1 database that is isolated from production and retain it as this Worker's shared Preview database.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>The shape of the change you're making:</p>
					<div class="cmd cmd--json">
						<div class="cmd-bar"><span class="cmd-label">wrangler.json</span></div>
						<pre><code>{`{
  "d1_databases": [
    { "binding": "DB", "database_name": "d1-template-database" } // production
  ],
  "previews": {
    "d1_databases": [
      { "binding": "DB", "database_name": "workshop-preview-db" }
    ],
    "observability": { "enabled": true }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
					</div>
					<p class="phase-note">Same binding name (<code>DB</code>), different database. This block will remain on <code>main</code> after the PR merges.</p>
					<PromptBlock label="Copy this prompt into your agent" text={PROMPTS.isolateResource} />
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p><code>wrangler.json</code> now points Previews at <code>workshop-preview-db</code>, enables Preview observability, leaves production untouched, and has the change committed.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<details class="aside">
				<summary>Why doesn't this apply to Durable Objects?</summary>
				<div class="aside-body">
					<p>
						Durable Objects and Containers are the actual exception. When the class lives in the same Worker, each Preview gets its own namespace and storage automatically — no override needed — because that state belongs to the Worker itself, not to an external resource identified by an ID. D1, KV, and R2 are the norm, not the exception: bind by ID, and anything sharing that ID shares the data.
					</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<div class="step-next">
				<a href="#preview" class="step-next-link">
					<span class="step-next-hint">Next</span>
					Open your Preview
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.isolate?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 3: Preview ─── */}
	<article id="preview" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(3).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(3).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(3).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Push the branch, open a pull request, and let Workers Builds run <code>wrangler preview</code>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Configure</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>In the Worker's <strong>Settings → Builds</strong> configuration, set the non-production branch/version command to <code>npx wrangler preview</code>. Keep the production deploy command unchanged.</p>
					<p class="phase-note">Deploy to Cloudflare currently configures branch builds with <code>npx wrangler versions upload</code>, which creates a version but not a branch Preview.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Ask your agent to push and open the PR:</p>
					<PromptBlock label="Copy this prompt into your agent" text={PROMPTS.openPullRequest} />
					<p class="phase-note">Within a minute or two, <strong>Workers Builds</strong> deploys the Preview and comments the URL directly on your pull request.</p>
					<Figure
						alt="A GitHub pull request with a Cloudflare Workers and Pages bot comment containing the Preview deployment URL."
						placeholderLabel="Placeholder — the Workers Builds bot comment on the PR, showing the Preview URL to click."
						caption="Where the Preview URL shows up. Click it to open your Preview in a new tab."
					/>
					<div class="tip">
						<span class="tip-label">Build or comment missing?</span>
						<p>If Workers Builds fails with API code <code>10015</code>, or no bot comment appears, run <code>npx wrangler preview</code> from the branch and open the printed <strong>Preview URL</strong>. This uses your Wrangler login while preserving the same branch Preview workflow.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Open the Preview URL from the PR. The page should render successfully and explain that the D1 binding exists but its schema has not been applied.</p>
					<Figure
						alt="The Preview Activity Log explaining that its connected D1 database needs the workshop schema."
						placeholderLabel="Preview setup state — the database is connected, but workshop/preview-schema.sql has not been applied."
						caption="A missing schema is an expected setup state, not a broken page."
					/>
					<div class="tip tip--pin">
						<span class="tip-label">Keep both tabs open</span>
						<p>Preview tab + production tab from Step 1. You'll flip between them in the next step.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="step-next">
				<a href="#interact" class="step-next-link">
					<span class="step-next-hint">Next</span>
					Apply the schema
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.preview?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 4: Prove ─── */}
	<article id="interact" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(4).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(4).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(4).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Apply a Preview-only candidate schema, then test the real user workflow.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>The SQL fixture lives outside <code>migrations/</code>, so production automation cannot discover it. Ask your agent to apply it to the Preview database by name:</p>
					<PromptBlock label="Copy this prompt into your agent" text={PROMPTS.applyPreviewSchema} />
					<p class="phase-note">Using the account-level database name rather than the <code>DB</code> binding is deliberate: the binding in top-level Wrangler configuration is production.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Refresh the Preview. It now shows three rows containing the word <strong>Preview</strong>. Add an entry and refresh: it persists. Click <strong>Delete</strong>: it fails and the page displays an error while preserving the row.</p>
					<Figure
						alt="The Preview Activity Log showing Preview-specific seed rows and a visible delete failure message."
						placeholderLabel="Preview after setup — Preview seed rows load, add and refresh work, and delete shows an error."
						caption="The candidate schema exposed a real compatibility bug without changing production."
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<details class="aside">
				<summary>Why does this matter?</summary>
				<div class="aside-body">
					<p>This is what "isolated environment for every change" actually means in practice — not a slide, a database you can watch stay separate while you poke at it.</p>
				</div>
			</details>

			<div class="step-next">
				<a href="#observability" class="step-next-link">
					<span class="step-next-hint">Next</span>
					Observability
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.interact?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 5: Observability ─── */}
	<article id="observability" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(5).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(5).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(5).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Use the failed request's structured log to find the schema mismatch.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>In the Cloudflare dashboard:</p>
					<ol class="steps-inline">
						<li>Go to <strong>Workers &amp; Pages</strong> → your Worker.</li>
						<li>Open the <strong>Observability</strong> tab (production view), then switch to <strong>Previews</strong> and select your branch.</li>
					</ol>
					<Figure
						alt="The Cloudflare dashboard Observability tab for the Worker, with the Previews view selected and the attendee's branch chosen from the selector."
						placeholderLabel="Placeholder — the dashboard: Workers & Pages → your Worker → Observability tab, with the Previews view and your branch selected."
						caption="The screen most people can't find on their own: switch from the production view to Previews, then pick your branch."
					/>
					<ol class="steps-inline" start="3">
						<li>Try Delete once more, then open the failed request in the log list.</li>
					</ol>
					<p class="phase-note">If your account does not show the Previews selector, continue by comparing the failing delete query in <code>src/index.ts</code> with <code>workshop/preview-schema.sql</code>. Preview log access is entitlement-dependent during the private beta.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Find <code>activity_log.delete_failed</code>. Its D1 error should identify the old column reference. Copy the error for your agent, or let an agent with Observability MCP access retrieve it.</p>
					<Figure
						alt="The Observability request list scoped to the Preview branch, showing only the requests made to the Preview URL, separate from production traffic."
						placeholderLabel="Placeholder — the per-branch request/log list, showing only your Preview's requests (not production's)."
						caption="Success looks like this: a request list scoped to your branch alone — separate logs and traces, same as the separate database."
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="step-next">
				<a href="#final" class="step-next-link">
					<span class="step-next-hint">Next</span>
					Fix and merge
					<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<article class="stepcard leader-card">
		<span class="leader-card-badge">🎤 For the room lead</span>
		<ul class="leader-card-list">
			{LEADER_NOTES.observability?.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}
		</ul>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Step 6: Fix and merge ─── */}
	<article id="final" class="stepcard">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">{stepByIndex(6).num}</span>
				<span class="stepcard-badge-time">{stepByIndex(6).time}</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">{stepByIndex(6).label}</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Repair the incompatibility, prove the Preview works, then promote only safe code.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Do</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<PromptBlock label="Give the error and this prompt to your agent" text={PROMPTS.diagnoseAndFix} />
					<p class="phase-note">A change from <code>id</code> to <code>activity_id</code> would only fix the Preview. The repair must also work with production's unchanged schema.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--verify">Verify</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<p>Wait for Workers Builds to update the same Preview URL. If you used the local fallback, run <code>npx wrangler preview</code> again instead. Add, refresh, and delete must all pass. Production should still show its original production rows.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="phase">
				<span class="phase-badge phase-badge--do">Merge</span>
				<div class="phase-content">
					<PromptBlock label="Copy this prompt into your agent" text={PROMPTS.mergePullRequest} />
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	{/* ─── Wrap-up ─── */}
	<article id="wrap-up" class="stepcard stepcard--wrapup">
		<div class="stepcard-head">
			<div class="stepcard-badge stepcard-badge--wrapup">
				<span class="stepcard-badge-num">✓</span>
			</div>
			<div class="stepcard-head-copy">
				<h2 class="stepcard-title">Clean up</h2>
				<p class="stepcard-lede">Know what persists after the pull request closes.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="stepcard-body">
			<p class="wrapup-p">The branch Preview can be removed after merge, but keep <code>workshop-preview-db</code>. Its binding is now part of <code>main</code> and it serves as the shared, production-safe database for future Previews. Those Previews are isolated from production but share this database with each other.</p>
			<details class="aside">
				<summary>Finished experimenting? Remove everything</summary>
				<div class="aside-body">
					<p>From the cloned repository, delete the Worker and both remote D1 databases, then optionally delete the GitHub repository:</p>
					<div class="cmd">
						<div class="cmd-bar"><span class="cmd-label">Terminal</span></div>
						<pre><code>npx wrangler delete
npx wrangler d1 delete workshop-preview-db
npx wrangler d1 delete &lt;production-database-name-from-wrangler.json&gt;</code></pre>
					</div>
					<p>Confirm the Worker and databases are gone in the Cloudflare dashboard. Delete the branch Preview there if it is still listed.</p>
				</div>
			</details>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

